CRITIQUE r1 claude-sonnet-5-5: 5 flaws in 14s, ~$0.0432
  flaw: Porch on core south was skipped because the core has an entrance on s but the ring sits against it, so no doorway exists on that wall.
    fix: Removed the core porch and put an industrial porch (size 2) on the ring's south side, where its entrance is.
  flaw: The bridge was skipped because the engine does not allow bridges onto a ring. The glass labs also sit on a 3-block yard that leaves them detached.
    fix: Set the glass_labs gap to 0 so it hugs the ring with a shared doorway, and removed the bridge.
  flaw: The landing pad was skipped because the pad_hall roof is too small, and the hall is a low box that adds nothing to the silhouette.
    fix: Widened pad_hall to 18x14 and moved the landing pad to the ring roof, which is 10 wide, so it is not skipped. A pad on the wider hall roof is more reliable.
  flaw: Orange stripe is barely visible: only small orange dots on the core, and none on the ring or the labs.
    fix: Set accent_floor to 0 on the ring and on glass_labs so the orange stripe reads across the whole station.
  flaw: The gray dome of deepslate-like blocks clashes with the white theme.
    fix: Gave the core a white concrete roof with a light gray trim so the dome reads white.
